4.2. Ideological Consensus and Dispersion Analysis
Reporting an association coefficient alone would obscure a distinction that matters for interpretation: the two sites differ not only in which ideology dominates, but in how much internal variation they contain. To quantify the degree of homogeneity within each site, the proportion of the modal category was examined alongside two dispersion metrics — normalized Shannon entropy on a 0–1 scale and Simpson's index of diversity (1 − Σpᵢ²) — with the three ideological labels treated as equally weighted categories.
